# Pull request notes

When you open a pull request, add its description to `docs/pull-requests/` in the same change.

- File name: `NNNN-short-title.md`, where `NNNN` is the pull request number, zero-padded to 4 digits. If the number is not known yet, use the next number after the highest file already in that folder, then rename once the pull request exists.
- Keep the documentation from the description: title, link to the pull request, summary, behavior, endpoints, and error cases.
- Leave out test plans, checklists, and tool footers.
- Add one row to `docs/pull-requests/README.md`.

```markdown
# Short title

[Pull request #15](https://github.com/markoilicni/experiment_api/pull/15)

## Summary

- What changed and how callers use it.
```
